      "about": "F&O stocks that opened at their low of the day so far and above yesterday's close, whose latest 3-min candle opened at its low and closed higher. The day's open, high and low are the exchange's, the pre-open price as the open. Differs from the usual form of this scan: F&O stocks in place of NIFTY 200; the 3-min lines judge each closed candle, not the one still forming; two lines, yesterday's close above its 200-day average and a 15-day average volume above 10 lakh, are written in and switched off until the history download; the body test, (close - open) / (close - low) of 0.7 or more, is written as close above open, which finds the same stocks while the 3-min open is its low and stops meaning the same if that line is switched off; ranked by the day's % change, largest first.",
